+# CVE-2026-64641 — Not applicable to next@13.3.0
+
+Advisory: GHSA-m99w-x7hq-7vfj (CWE-834, Uncontrolled Recursion / excessive
+iteration)
+Upstream fix: vercel/next.js commit
+019628571641dec57aaf349ba0c360e3964e6f12 (PR #96013)
+
+## Summary
+
+This is a documentation-only marker. next@13.3.0 does **not** contain the
+vulnerable code path, so no functional change is required.
+
+## Analysis
+
+The vulnerability is an unbounded iteration over `$ACTION_REF_`-prefixed
+form fields inside `areAllActionIdsValid()`, which is reached only through
+the multi-page-application (MPA) server-action form-decode path
+(`decodeAction`) in
+`packages/next/src/server/app-render/action-handler.ts`.
+
+The `decodeAction` MPA form-decode subsystem — along with
+`areAllActionIdsValid()` and the `$ACTION_REF_` form-field handling that the
+fix bounds — was introduced in next v13.4.0 (PR #49187). None of these
+symbols exist anywhere in the 13.3.0 source tree.
+
+At v13.3.0, `handleAction()` decodes a single action id via `decodeReply`
+and has no `$ACTION_REF_` iteration loop, so the excessive-iteration
+condition addressed by the fix cannot occur.
+
+## Disposition
+
+Target version 13.3.0 predates the introduction of the vulnerable mechanism
+(v13.4.0). No backport is possible or necessary; the upstream fix commit has
+nothing to attach to at this version. This marker records the
+version-boundary determination.

